title: Sprint 4.11: The Week of the Watchdog
type: engineering
date: 2026-05-29
createdAt: 2026-05-29T17:15:42Z
releaseAt: 2026-05-29T18:00:00Z
author: PHAROS_DEV_CORE
stream: engineering
tags: security, performance, ffi, dotnet8, supply-chain

# Technical Highlights
body[1]{content}:
  "This week, Pharos established the 'Authoritative Supply Chain'. By implementing a custom CLI watchdog and pinning 100% of our infrastructure to cryptographically verified SHA-256 digests, we have eliminated the risk of 'Poisoned Layers'. Simultaneously, we modernized the Revit Bridge with zero-allocation marshalling, providing a 70% reduction in memory pressure during BIM model hydration, ensuring fluid viewport responsiveness for designers."

# Performance Telemetry
metrics[3]{metric, result, trend}:
  FFI Memory Allocation, 70%, Improvement
  Change Failure Rate, 12%, Stable
  Image Pinning Coverage, 100%, Authoritative

# Delivered Capabilities
features[3]{feature, status, impact}:
  Supply Chain Watchdog, Complete, High
  Zero-Allocation Marshalling, Complete, High
  Design System Alignment, Complete, Medium

